+The world design that the generated-maps steps (the G series on the [Roadmap](Roadmap)) are building toward. It comes from the [procedural maps options doc](https://claude.ai/artifact/7qncafySjNAx8pW92fVcXg), whose 16 review decisions are recorded in its "Decisions from review" table and in the [requirements](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/blob/main/docs/requirements.md) under "World structure: a day on the line". These are initial picks to build and playtest, not final.
+
+## Three time scales
+
+- **A train:** one robbery, a few minutes. It ends when the train reaches the next town, you get off, or you're thrown off.
+- **A day:** a run, about 12 minutes from dawn to dusk, with several trains passing.
+- **A career:** many days, until your outlaw dies (permadeath is a variant).
+
+## The world
+
+The world is one seeded railway that runs on forever, with terrain around it, towns every few thousand tiles and trains on a seeded timetable. You find the track, scout or wait, and pick a train, sometimes the wrong or a tougher one. You find trains by their smoke and whistles, and tell train types apart by sight once there are several types; later by rumours and timetables too. At dusk you pick a camp off the line, and tomorrow starts from there. Each career gets a new world.
+
+Trains run one way first, and both ways once passing loops exist. Forks come later, leading into regions with different trains. Something has to stop you riding off the side of the line: see [Map edges](Map-edges).
+
+## How the clocks fit together
+
+The day clock budgets the whole day, and riding to a train and scouting use part of it. Once you're aboard, the train clock counts down to the next town, where the law gets on, so town spacing sets how long one robbery can last. Train length (cars and loot) has to fit that time. Town spacing, train speed and cars per train are tuned together, starting from the Phase 2 target robbery time.
+
+## Daily and friends
+
+The free demo is a daily day: everyone gets the same seed, with a streak, a wanted poster and a community line that everyone moves along together. Your record carries into the full game when you buy it. Owners can ride the daily as a gang with friends who don't own the game, and the occasional free gang weekend lets free players ride together. Ghost riders were declined.
