+An idea page under [Ideas](Ideas): what stops you riding off the side of the line on generated maps. The first edges are scheduled with G10 on the [Roadmap](Roadmap); the rest wait for the systems they need.
+
+## The idea
+
+Something has to stop you riding off the side of the line, with no invisible walls and no warning popups. The pick is that each region chooses its own edge, and the two sides of the line can be different: a canyon region could have a mesa wall on one side and a great river on the other. You should be able to see an edge coming before you reach it: heat shimmer over the desert, a line of mesas on the horizon, the sound of the river. Camps sit inside the edges.
+
+## First edges, with G10
+
+The first edges come in G10, because the map already has everything they need (deep water, cliffs, blocked, slow and mud ground):
+
+| Edge | How it stops you | Kind |
+|---|---|---|
+| Great river | Wide deep water, with fords only near the line | Hard wall |
+| Mesa wall | A long cliff or row of mesas blocks the whole side | Hard wall |
+| Mountain range | Snowy peaks rise to impassable rock | Hard wall |
+| Deep canyon | A gorge runs beside the line; the far rim can't be reached | Hard wall |
+| Badlands | Broken ground, mud and rock: very slow, and nothing out there | Soft |
+| Marsh or bog | Mud everywhere slows you to a crawl | Soft |
+
+## Later edges
+
+The others need systems that come later, so they arrive with those:
+
+| Edge | How it stops you | Arrives with |
+|---|---|---|
+| Endless desert | No water; your horse tires and slows until it won't go on | A horse stamina step after G10 |
+| Dense forest | Slow riding, and the trees hide train smoke on the horizon | G10, since G9 (before it) adds the smoke it hides |
+| Salt flats | Fast and open, but with no cover chasers spot you from far off | Pinkertons, after Phase 3 |
+| The law's reach | The further from the line, the more posses ride | G11-G12 (bounty hunters, wanted level per region) |
+| Ranch land, army territory | Fences and ranchers who shoot; patrols that raise your wanted level | After Phase 3 combat |
+| Wild animals | Wolves or rattlesnakes spook the horse and can throw you | After G10 (a horse spook and throw) |
+| Dust storm wall | A storm front you can't see or steer in turns you back | Weather or night, after G8 |
+
+## Pinkertons
+
+Pinkertons aren't scheduled yet. They need guards who ride and fight, so they come with or after Phase 3 combat, and they get better with G10's terrain.
+
