+Riding as a gang with friends is part of the plan from the start ("multiplayer-ready by design" in the [requirements](https://github.com/devlinjunker/train-robber/blob/main/docs/requirements.md)). Where it lands in the build order is on the [Roadmap](Roadmap).
+
+## Two steps
+
+Decided 2026-10-27:
+- **A network test right after Phase 3.** Two players on one train through a simple server, with no lobby. Combat is the hardest part to get right over a network (shots, melee, guards reacting to several players), so it gets tested as soon as it exists. The test keeps running as Phases 4 and 5 add the passenger and bank trains, so each new train is checked over the network as it's built.
+- **Full multiplayer later.** Lobbies, accounts, lag handling and the rest.
+
+## Already in place
+
+These have been in the sim since Phase 0, so adding multiplayer later isn't a rewrite:
+- Every command and everything a player owns carries a player id. The run state is split into shared parts (countdown, heat, the train) and per-player parts (health, carried loot).
+- The game logic has no global state, so one server can host several games.
+- Commands are stamped with the tick they happen on, and the host owns the clock.
+- The state is plain data, so snapshots are cheap to send.
+- The model is a server in charge with prediction on each player's machine (not lockstep), so small differences between browsers only cause small corrections.
+
+## Still to build
+
+Sending the game over the network, lobbies, handling lag, cheat protection, accounts and per-player saves.
+
+## Open design questions
+
+How loot is split, whose heat counts, and where saves live once there are accounts.
+
+## Where it shows up
+
+- **After Phase 3:** the network test, kept working through Phases 4 and 5.
+- **Full online multiplayer:** after Phase 5 and the daily day (G15).
+- **G15, the daily day:** owners can ride the daily as a gang with friends who don't own the game, and an occasional free gang weekend lets free players ride together.
+- **G16, shared world online:** your gang shares one day and camp, a server checks the chunks near each player, and Pinkertons split up to chase each player.
